Explanation: The comment "some account of "frm" has more money than "amnt"" essentially asserts that the balance of some account of the sender (frm) is greater than the amount to be transferred (amnt). However, if "frm" is equal to "to" (i.e., the sender and the receiver are the same person), we should allow this condition to be true because a transfer to the same account is not meaningful in terms of money transfer, although it would decrease the balance. That's why we have the second part of the condition in the assert statement: `True` in this case.
